content.text:
The investigation points to one root cause: search's calls to rate fail almost immediately, and that propagates to the frontend's `/hotels` route. I did not run a network-level check, so the DNS-versus-partition choice is an inference from the failure timing.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "dns_lookup_failed",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT count(*) FILTER (WHERE attr_status_code='Error' AND duration<1e6) AS fast_errors_under_1ms, count(*) FILTER (WHERE attr_status_code='Error' AND duration>=1e9) AS slow_errors_over_1s, count(*) AS total FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' AND attr_span_kind='Client'", "claim": "Nearly all search→rate.GetRates client calls fail in under 1 ms; only two take about 20 s."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='rate' GROUP BY 1,2,3 UNION ALL SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='rate' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Rate server spans drop from hundreds per period to about 2 in the abnormal window while the pod stays running."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name pod, metric, count(*) n, max(value) max_value FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'rate%' AND metric IN ('k8s.container.restarts','k8s.pod.uptime') GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Rate pod shows no restarts and no uptime reset, so rate itself was not restarting during the incident."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "search", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT p.service_name parent_svc, c.service_name child_svc, c.span_name, c.attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces p ON c.parent_span_id = p.span_id AND c.trace_id = p.trace_id WHERE p.service_name='frontend' AND c.service_name='search' GROUP BY 1,2,3,4", "claim": "Frontend calls to search.Search/Nearby return Error on all 301 requests, which become HTTP 500 on /hotels."}]}
  ]
}
```
